# arvo-digest

A digest of explicit bytes, at a width the type names. Not cryptographic.

Two algorithms by name, `Fnv1a` at 32 and 64 bits and `Xxh3` at 64 and 128 bits, and one switched
digest, `Digest::<64>::of`, which runs FNV-1a on short input and XXH3 from a measured length on. Every
path has a `const fn` form that gives the same value as the runtime one, and a digest narrows into
`arvo_bits::Bits<N>` when the width a consumer pins it to is smaller.

Input is `arvo_numeral::Bytes` and the digest a host `Word` from the same crate, so no host integer is
named here. Depends on `arvo-numeral`, `arvo-bits` and on `xxhash-rust` for XXH3. `no_std`, no allocation.

## Status

Unreleased, at 0.0.0. The source implements what is described here and its tests pass, and the surface
may still change before a first release.
